arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-393b30ac7f274207a838e4c4c010bc81/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`.

The project structure:
- `ShipmentTracker/` - Server project (hosts app, EF Core, Identity, API endpoints)
- `ShipmentTracker.Client/` - Client project (all interactive components, pages)

**Key architecture rule**: Interactive components live in `.Client`. They cannot access DbContext directly. Data access pattern:
1. Define interface in `.Client` project
2. Client implements it with HttpClient calling server APIs
3. Server implements it with direct EF Core access
4. Register both in respective Program.cs files
5. Server exposes minimal API endpoints

## What to implement

### 1. Remove template pages
Delete these files from `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`:
- `Counter.razor`
- `Weather.razor`

### 2. Create the Shipment model in Client project
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### 3. Create IShipmentService interface in Client project
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<Shipment?> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
    Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment);
}
```

### 4. Create HttpClient-based implementation in Client project
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService : IShipmentService
{
    private readonly HttpClient _http;

    public ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http)
    {
        _http = http;
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await _http.GetAsync($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var response = await _http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        var response = await _http.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>())!;
    }
}
```

### 5. Create EF Core entity and DbContext extension on the server
The server project already has `Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs`. Add a `Shipment` entity there.

Create `ShipmentTracker/Data/ShipmentEntity.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class ShipmentEntity
{
    public int Id { get; set; }

    [MaxLength(50)]
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    public int Status { get; set; }

    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }

    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }

    [MaxLength(256)]
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(500)]
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

Read the existing `ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs` file and add a `DbSet<ShipmentEntity> Shipments` property to it.

### 6. Create server-side IShipmentService implementation
Create `ShipmentTracker/Services/ShipmentServerService.cs`:
```csharp
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Data;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Services;

public class ShipmentServerService : IShipmentService
{
    private readonly ApplicationDbContext _db;

    public ShipmentServerService(ApplicationDbContext db)
    {
        _db = db;
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await _db.Shipments
            .OrderByDescending(s => s.CreatedAt)
            .Select(s => MapToModel(s))
            .ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var entity = await _db.Shipments
            .FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);
        return entity == null ? null : MapToModel(entity);
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var entity = await _db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);
        if (entity == null) return null;
        entity.Status = (int)status;
        await _db.SaveChangesAsync();
        return MapToModel(entity);
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        var entity = new ShipmentEntity
        {
            TrackingNumber = GenerateTrackingNumber(),
            Origin = shipment.Origin,
            Destination = shipment.Destination,
            Status = (int)ShipmentStatus.Pending,
            EstimatedDelivery = shipment.EstimatedDelivery,
            CreatedAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
            CustomerEmail = shipment.CustomerEmail,
            Description = shipment.Description
        };
        _db.Shipments.Add(entity);
        await _db.SaveChangesAsync();
        return MapToModel(entity);
    }

    private static Shipment MapToModel(ShipmentEntity entity) => new()
    {
        Id = entity.Id,
        TrackingNumber = entity.TrackingNumber,
        Origin = entity.Origin,
        Destination = entity.Destination,
        Status = (ShipmentStatus)entity.Status,
        EstimatedDelivery = entity.EstimatedDelivery,
        CreatedAt = entity.CreatedAt,
        CustomerEmail = entity.CustomerEmail,
        Description = entity.Description
    };

    private static string GenerateTrackingNumber()
    {
        return $"SHP-{DateTime.UtcNow:yyyyMMdd}-{Random.Shared.Next(100000, 999999)}";
    }
}
```

### 7. Create API endpoints
Create `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentEndpoints.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

namespace ShipmentTracker;

public static class ShipmentEndpoints
{
    public static void MapShipmentEndpoints(this WebApplication app)
    {
        var group = app.MapGroup("api/shipments");

        group.MapGet("/", async (IShipmentService service) =>
            Results.Ok(await service.GetAllShipmentsAsync()))
            .RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapGet("/track/{trackingNumber}", async (string trackingNumber, IShipmentService service) =>
        {
            var shipment = await service.GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(trackingNumber);
            return shipment is null ? Results.NotFound() : Results.Ok(shipment);
        }).RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapPut("/{id}/status", async (int id, ShipmentStatus status, IShipmentService service) =>
        {
            var shipment = await service.UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(id, status);
            return shipment is null ? Results.NotFound() : Results.Ok(shipment);
        }).RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapPost("/", async (Shipment shipment, IShipmentService service) =>
        {
            var created = await service.CreateShipmentAsync(shipment);
            return Results.Created($"api/shipments/track/{created.TrackingNumber}", created);
        }).RequireAuthorization();
    }
}
```

### 8. Update server Program.cs
Add to the server `Program.cs`:
- `using ShipmentTracker;` and `using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;` and `using ShipmentTracker.Services;` at the top (or inline)
- After the Identity service registrations, add: `builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentServerService>();`
- Before `app.Run();`, add: `app.MapShipmentEndpoints();`

### 9. Update client Program.cs
Update `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` to register the HttpClient and ShipmentHttpService:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress) });
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentHttpService>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

### 10. Create Pages in Client project

**Update `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Home.razor`** to be a landing page:
```razor
@page "/"

<PageTitle>ShipmentTracker - Home</PageTitle>

<h1>Shipment Tracker</h1>
<p>Welcome to the logistics shipment tracking system.</p>

<AuthorizeView>
    <Authorized>
        <div class="row mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h5 class="card-title">Dispatch Dashboard</h5>
                        <p class="card-text">View and manage all shipments, update statuses, and create new shipments.</p>
                        <a href="/shipments" class="btn btn-primary">Go to Dashboard</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h5 class="card-title">Track a Shipment</h5>
                        <p class="card-text">Enter a tracking number to check shipment status and estimated delivery.</p>
                        <a href="/track" class="btn btn-outline-primary">Track Shipment</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
